    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.visits\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nI can not find in docs, is there a way to set prompt? I find mini.visits very flexible for creation of custom mappings, but i think it is useful to modify vim.ui.select prompt.\r\n\r\nIf this feature is not there, maybe add new parameter in function/field in opts for MiniVisits.select_path/select_label commands?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.visits</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I can not find in docs, is there a way to set prompt? I find mini.visits very flexible for creation of custom mappings, but i think it is useful to modify vim.ui.select prompt.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If this feature is not there, maybe add new parameter in function/field in opts for MiniVisits.select_path/select_label commands?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.visits\nQuestion\nI can not find in docs, is there a way to set prompt? I find mini.visits very flexible for creation of custom mappings, but i think it is useful to modify vim.ui.select prompt.\nIf this feature is not there, maybe add new parameter in function/field in opts for MiniVisits.select_path/select_label commands?",
